node_modules
release
dist
supabase
tools
*.log

# Desktop installers are hosted on GitHub Releases, not here.
# Vercel rejects files at this size (~99 MB), and serving them from static
# hosting also billed every desktop download against the web app's bandwidth.
# latest.yml stays on this domain and points at the GitHub asset URL.
public/updates/*.exe
public/updates/*.exe.blockmap
public/updates/tauri/*.exe

# Build output that must never reach the deploy payload.
# src-tauri/target is 5.7 GB of Rust artifacts and contains individual .rlib
# files over 100 MB, which Vercel rejects outright. This was the real cause of
# "File size limit exceeded" — it appeared after the Tauri migration started
# and nothing excluded it.
src-tauri
android
dist-tauri
dist-mobile
build
e2e
test-results
playwright-report
